I used to, once upon a time, and this is why:

I believed I learned more than I would through explore mode.  Some
monsters, I would just keep hitting the "n" key over and over again as
it killed me continuously.

What I preferred to do instead was save just BEFORE I tackled a nasty
situation. Then, if I die, re-load, and think "How could I have done
this differently?"  Then try the new strategy. Rinse and repeat  until
success.

I believed this gave me more practice and assisted me in finding the
"right" answer. It's the same principle as working and re-working a
math problem until one gets it right.

Of course, after a few scummed ascensions I threw away the crutch and
started doing it for real. All my YAAPs posted here were done
completely legitimately. 

